# text = Are you the poet I -- I do a little in that way Ah ! poetry makes life what light and music do the stage -- strip the one of the false embellishments , and the other of its illusions , and what is there real in either to live or care for Very true , Sir To be before the footlights is like sitting at a grand court show , and admiring the silken dresses of the gaudy throng ; to be behind them is to be the people who make that finery , uncared for and unknown , and left to sink or swim , to starve or live , as fortune wills it Certainly Go on , Jemmy like black-eyed Susan -- all in the Downs -- no croaking -- speak out -- look lively
