# text = The man of whom I speak was a low pantomime actor ; and , like many people of his class , an habitual drunkard . in his better days , before he had become enfeebled by dissipation and emaciated by disease , he had been in the receipt of a good salary , which , if he had been careful and prudent , he might have continued to receive for some years -- not many ; because these men either die early , or by unnaturally taxing their bodily energies , lose , prematurely , those physical powers on which alone they can depend for subsistence .
