# text = If ever I meet that man again , I'll Yes , yes that's all very well ; but while we stand talking here , they'll get their licence , and be married in London How far is it to the next stage Six mile , ain't it , Tom Rayther better Rayther better nor six mile , Sir Can't be helped we must walk it , Pickwick No help for it Sam Hollo Number twenty-two wants his boots Ask number twenty-two , vether he'll have 'em now , or vait till he gets 'em Come , don't be a fool , Sam the gentleman wants his boots directly Well , you ARE a nice young ' ooman for a musical party , you are Sam where's that lazy , idle -- why , Sam -- oh , there you are ; why don't you answer Vouldn't be gen-teel to answer , till you'd done talking Here , clean these shoes for number seventeen directly , and take 'em to private sitting-room , number five , first floor Number five She came in early this morning with a gentleman in a hackney-coach , and it's him as wants his boots , and you'd better do 'em , that's all about it Vy didn't you say so before Come in Boots Sir Do you know -- what's a-name -- Doctors' Commons Yes , Sir Where is it Paul's Churchyard , Sir ; low archway on the carriage side , bookseller's at one corner , hot-el on the other , and two porters in the middle as touts for licences Touts for licences Touts for licences
