# text = Glancing at all these things with the air of a man who had seen them too often before , to think them worthy of much notice now , my uncle walked up the middle of the street , with a thumb in each waistcoat pocket , indulging from time to time in various snatches of song , chanted forth with such good-will and spirit , that the quiet honest folk started from their first sleep and lay trembling in bed till the sound died away in the distance ; when , satisfying themselves that it was only some drunken ne'er-do-weel finding his way home , they covered themselves up warm and fell asleep again .
