# text = The doors had been torn from their hinges and removed ; the linings had been stripped off , only a shred hanging here and there by a rusty nail ; the lamps were gone , the poles had long since vanished , the ironwork was rusty , the paint was worn away ; the wind whistled through the chinks in the bare woodwork ; and the rain , which had collected on the roofs , fell , drop by drop , into the insides with a hollow and melancholy sound .
